#
# PURPOSE:
#   This is a Terraform module that encapsulates Databricks workspace configuration.
#   Modules are reusable components that can be called from other Terraform
#   configurations. This module handles all Databricks-specific resources.
#
# KEY CONCEPTS FOR BEGINNERS:
#   - Modules: Reusable Terraform configurations that can be called like functions
#   - Module structure: Similar to root modules (variables, resources, outputs)
#   - Module benefits: Reusability, organization, abstraction
#   - Module usage: Called from root module using module blocks
#
# TERRAFORM DOCUMENTATION:
#   - Modules: https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/modules
#   - Module Composition: https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/modules/develop
#   - Module Structure: https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/modules/develop/structure
#
# HOW MODULES WORK:
#   1. This module defines inputs (variables) and outputs
#   2. Root modules call this module: module "databricks" { source = "./modules/databricks" }
#   3. Root modules pass values to module variables
#   4. Module creates resources and returns outputs
#   5. Root modules can use module outputs
# ============================================================================

